==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Alternative forms===
* [[trap door]]
* [[trap-door]]

===Etymology===
{{term|trap}} + {{term|door}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[hinged]] or [[sliding]] [[door]] set into a [[floor]] or [[ceiling]].
# {{label|en|theater}} Such a [[trap]] set into the floor of a [[stage]] to allow fast [[exit]]s and [[entrance]]s.
# {{label|en|computing}} A [[secret]] method of obtaining [[access]] to a [[program]] or [[online]] [[system]]; a [[backdoor]].
# {{label|en|mathematics|cryptography}} The special information that permits the [[inverse]] of a [[trapdoor function]] to be easily computed.
# {{label|en|mining}} A door in a [[level]] for regulating the ventilating current; [[weather door]].
#: {{rfquotek|Raymond}}

